r.summary:
The bot is idle most of the time. The live settings hold cash 95.5% (2021-23) and 97.1% (2024-26) of the time on average, all-cash in 84–90% of hours; the concentrated settings 77–90%. Parking that cash in a halal spot engine (sold when bids need money) does add some return, but it does not reach 10%/month honestly.

The design chosen on 2021-23 data only, from 884 pre-registered runs, is 2 coins x 50%, +5% take-profit, plus BTC held while above its 50-day average, sold by a watcher within 2% of a trigger, with a 7-day re-buy wait. It made:
- 2024-26: +6.11%/month, drop -33.9% (without parking: +5.53%, -28.7%);
- since 2025: +3.57%/month, drop -29.0% (without: +2.66%);
- 2021-23: +14.48%/month, drop -49.6%;
- under 0.2% worse fills + LUNA/FTT/SRM: +3.99% in 2024-26 (without parking: +4.09%), so the gain disappears.

For the live 8-coin bot, the same rule picks BTC/ETH 50-day parking (open-only arming within 5%, 7-day re-buy wait):
- +4.74%/month in 2024-26 vs +2.89%;
- +5.18% since 2025 vs +1.96%;
- 2021-23 stress drop -59% vs -40%.

Only hindsight reaches 10%. With 1 coin x 100% plus ETH held while above its 30–70-day average, 2024-26 makes 10.1–10.65%/month with about a -50% drop. Even with hindsight, the best parking setting in the pre-registered grids was 9.95%. It could not have been chosen from 2021-23: ETH parking alone made +0.25%/month then, and that base's 2021-23 drop was -61%. It also falls to about 4.5–5.3%/month with fills 0.2% worse, and loses 100% in 2021-23 once LUNA is included.

Parking rotated by momentum among the 19 coins was ruinous (drops -55% to -100%). Even with free parking trades the honest pick would reach only 6.51%/month.

Bottom line: idle cash is worth about +0.6 to +1.9 points/month on 2024-26 backtests, mostly from BTC/ETH trend, and costs deeper drops and fragility to fills. It is not the route to 10%.

critic.verified:
I re-ran the key designs. Every number in this answer comes from these runs; logs are in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-halal-rider/ec562e35-ea9e-5a74-ab92-4ff22c5eeb77/scratchpad/pb_out_x10/critic/ (check.log, critic_velocity.log, critic_wicks.log, critic_universe.log, critic_idle.log).

1. Kernel copy. I copied the velocity agent's 1-minute kernel and added switches for order delay and minute-level watch mode (x10_critic_lib.xkernel). With the new switches off it reproduces vkernel exactly: identical trade logs and zero equity difference in 14 cases (19 and 22 coins, picks, hindsight designs, stressed fills). Minute-level watch mode, with positions that never compete for cash, gives the same trades as the universe agent's hourly watch kernel (4 cases).

2. Velocity. All four reports and worst trades match the agent's log to 0.01 point, for:
   - live settings (+2.89%/month, drop -16%);
   - the 2-coin hourly pick (+5.52%);
   - round-1 pick (+6.32%/month, drop -27%; since 2025 +3.72%; 2021-23 +16.13%, drop -45%; stressed with LUNA/FTT/SRM: +3.87 / +2.23 / +8.44, drop -62%);
   - round-2 pick (+5.81% / +4.34%);
   - round-3 pick (+9.23% / +7.72%);
   - hindsight best (+11.71% / +10.06%, drop -39%; 2021-23 drop -97% with LUNA);
   - LUNA-surviving variant (+10.51% / +8.65%).

3. Idle-cash honest pick reproduced exactly: +6.11%/month (drop -33.9%), since 2025 +3.57%, 2021-23 +14.48%; stressed +3.99 / +1.69 / +7.40. Its base without parking: +5.53%; stressed +4.09%.

4. Universe H4 design reproduced: +11.04% / +8.56% / +14.71% (drop -63%). Their stress (adversarial order plus 0.3% extra slippage) +8.14%, bid mode +8.19%. The 19-coin core in hourly watch mode gives +10.52% on hourly candles built from the minute data (agent: +10.51%).

5. Code read for lookahead and funding: all five kernels plus the cycle bar builder. Every trigger reference is shifted to closed candles. Decisions use the bar or minute open. Resting bids are reserved from cash, watch-mode buys use cash on hand, and parking is sold before a bid is funded. All four other agents' equivalence logs pass.

6. Screened coins: the universe agent's loader keeps only coins in code/universe.py pass_map. FTT, which is not screened, appears only in stress runs. The other agents use the 19 live coins, plus LUNA/FTT/SRM in stress runs.

finalists.how_to_run:
Hourly holdout (16 live coins), 3 variants:
- research/panic_buyer/refine/x10_universe_lib.urun(P, idx, slip, N=1, fmax=1.0, depth=0.14, tp=0.05, hm=48, cd=24, smult=guard, watch=True), where guard = ((cf / cf.rolling(168, min_periods=1).max() - 1) >= -0.35).shift(1, fill_value=True) as a float mask (x10_universe_push2.guard_mask logic);
- the same with worder=1 (adversarial order);
- engine.run(P, idx, depth=0.14, N=1, fmax=1.0, tp=0.05, hm=48, cd=24, smult=guard) (bid mechanism).
If 2018-20 1-minute data exist, use x10_critic_lib.xrun(A, hidx, Ph, SLIP, K, ref=x10_critic_lib.guard_ref(Ph, 0.35, K), N=1, fmax=1.0, depth=0.14, tp=0.05, hm=48, cd=24, watch=1, cyc=60). The full H4 (top-50 tier at +6 points depth and half size) needs 2018-20 volume files for the screened coins: x10_critic_universe.run.
